sequenceDiagram
    participant A as User A (pays 5M)
    participant B as User B (pays 5M)
    participant PS as Payment Service
    participant FS as Fee Service
    participant US as User Service
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ

    par User A's transaction arrives first
        A->>PS: POST /transactions (mssv=X, amount=5000000)
        PS->>FS: reserve fee (mssv=X)
        FS->>FS: findOneAndUpdate({mssv=X, status="chua_thanh_toan"},<br/>{status="dang_xu_ly"})
        Note over FS: Condition is inside the filter -> atomic.<br/>Only one request can match the document.
        FS-->>PS: 200 OK - fee reserved
        PS->>US: deduct balance (userA, 5000000)
        US-->>PS: 200 OK - balance deducted
        PS-->>A: 201 Created - OTP sent
        A->>PS: POST /transactions/:id/verify-otp
        PS->>FS: confirm payment (mssv=X)
        FS->>FS: status = "da_thanh_toan", paid_amount += 5000000
        FS-->>PS: 200 OK
        PS->>MQ: confirmation email event (via OTP Service)
        PS-->>A: 200 OK - transaction success
    and User B's transaction arrives almost same time
        B->>PS: POST /transactions (mssv=X, amount=5000000)
        PS->>FS: reserve fee (mssv=X)
        FS->>FS: findOneAndUpdate({mssv=X, status="chua_thanh_toan"}, ...)
        Note over FS: status is already "dang_xu_ly" (reserved by A)<br/>-> no document matches
        FS-->>PS: 409 Conflict - fee being processed or already paid
        PS-->>B: 409 Conflict - "Học phí đang được xử lý hoặc đã thanh toán"
        Note over B: User B is NOT charged.<br/>No compensating transaction needed<br/>because rejection happened BEFORE deducting balance.
    end

    Note over A,MQ: If deducting User A's balance had FAILED instead,<br/>Payment Service would call FS to UNDO the reservation<br/>(compensating transaction) so User B could retry.
